<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:</strong></span></td><td>Gause&#39;s competitive exclusion principle states that two closely related species competing for different resources cannot exist indefinitely.</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td>According to Gause&#39;s principle, during competition, the inferior will be eliminated. This may be true if resources are limiting.</td></tr></tbody></table>
In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I</strong> and <strong>Statement II</strong> are False.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td><strong>Statement I </strong>is True&nbsp;but&nbsp;<strong>Statement II</strong> is False.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is False but <strong>Statement II</strong> is True.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I</strong> and <strong>Statement II</strong> are True.</td></tr></tbody></table>

